Hi,

I'm encountering a segmentation fault when running a UML kernel
compiled with GCOV profiling enabled.

My steps:

1. Create .config using make ARCH=um defconfig
and config the following flags:

CONFIG_GCOV_KERNEL=y
CONFIG_ARCH_HAS_GCOV_PROFILE_ALL=y
CONFIG_GCOV_PROFILE_ALL=y

2. Compile to UML kernel

3. run ./linux --help will result in

~/UML/linux-6.13.1$ ./linux --help
Segmentation fault (core dumped)

4. Even not config CONFIG_GCOV_PROFILE_ALL,
adding GCOV_PROFILE := y to subdirectory's Makefile(s) will cause
same Segmentation fault error.

5. The issue disappears when totally disabling CONFIG_GCOV_PROFILE_ALL
Specifically,
With CONFIG_GCOV_PROFILE_ALL=y
~/UML/linux-6.13.1$ ./linux --help
Segmentation fault (core dumped)

Without CONFIG_GCOV_PROFILE_ALL=y
~/UML/linux-6.13.1$ ./linux --help
User Mode Linux v6.13.1
    available at http://user-mode-linux.sourceforge.net/
....


6. I tried with version 6.13.1, 6.1.44, 6.1.128,
and they also have this problem.

Any debugging suggestions would be greatly appreciated.
Thank you for your time and expertise.

Thanks,
Mingrui

Compiler:  gcc --version
gcc (Ubuntu 11.4.0-1ubuntu1~22.04) 11.4.0

Host System: Ubuntu 22.04.4 LTS
Host System kernel: 5.15.0-102-generic

